# Project Blueprint — React Native Expo Application

This rule defines the full architecture, project structure, coding standards, and patterns for this application. Follow every section precisely when generating, modifying, or reviewing code.

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Framework | React Native + Expo SDK (latest stable) | Managed workflow, new architecture enabled |
| Language | TypeScript (strict mode) | No `any` types unless absolutely unavoidable |
| Routing | Expo Router (file-based) | Typed routes enabled |
| State (global) | Redux Toolkit | Minimal — auth/session state only |
| State (local) | Custom hooks + useState | All page/feature logic lives in hooks |
| API | GraphQL (Hasura) | Queries and mutations in dedicated folders |
| Auth | Supabase Auth (PKCE) | Session persistence via AsyncStorage |
| Real-time | GraphQL subscriptions (graphql-ws) | WebSocket with auto-reconnect |
| Styling | React Native StyleSheet | Theme-aware via `createStyles(theme)` |
| i18n | i18next + react-i18next | Locale files in `/locales` |
| Error tracking | Sentry | Wraps root layout, traces GraphQL |
| Testing | Jest + React Testing Library | Tests in `/__tests__` |

