## Authentication Flow

1. App starts → Supabase checks for existing session
2. Auth state listener initialized in root layout
3. If no session → show login screen (conditional route)
4. On login → `supabase.auth.signInWithPassword()`
5. Session created → dispatch `authenticate` to Redux
6. Fetch user profile → store in Redux
7. Set Sentry user context
8. Register push notification token
9. Navigate to `/(tabs)/home`
10. On logout → clear push token, AsyncStorage, Redux state

### Auth Hook

```typescript
// hooks/auth/useAuth.ts — wraps Supabase + Redux
export default function useAuth() {
  const { user_id, userData, token, isAuthenticated } = useAppSelector(
    (state) => state.login
  )
  // ... login, logout, session refresh methods
  return { user_id, userData, token, isAuthenticated, login, logout }
}
```

