## TypeScript Guidelines

### Type Location

- ALL types in `/types` directory
- Barrel export from `/types/index.ts`
- One file per domain (`users.ts`, `posts.ts`, `events.ts`)

### Type Patterns

```typescript
// types/posts.ts
export interface Post {
  id: string
  title: string
  content: string
  author_id: string
  created_at: string
}

export type PostType = 'personal' | 'club' | 'event'

export enum PostPrivacy {
  Public = 'public',
  Private = 'private',
  FriendsOnly = 'friends_only',
}
```

### Inference Rules

```typescript
// Let TS infer when obvious
const [count, setCount] = useState(0)         // inferred as number
const items = data?.posts || []                // inferred from data

// Explicit when not obvious
function calculateTotal(items: Item[]): number { ... }
const handleUpdate = useCallback(async (userId: string, updates: Partial<User>): Promise<boolean> => { ... }, [])
```

### Strict Rules

- `strict: true` in tsconfig
- No `any` — use `unknown` and narrow
- Interfaces for object shapes, types for unions/primitives
- All function parameters explicitly typed
- Path alias: `@/*` → `./*`

