## Naming Conventions

### Files

| Type | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Components | PascalCase | `PostCard.tsx` |
| Hooks | camelCase with `use` prefix | `useHomePage.ts` |
| Queries | camelCase with `get` prefix | `getNotifications.ts` |
| Mutations | camelCase with verb prefix | `createPost.ts` |
| Types | camelCase | `users.ts` |
| Utilities | camelCase | `formatDate.ts` |
| Styles | match parent + `.styles.ts` | `index.styles.ts` |

### Variables

```typescript
// Booleans: is, has, should, can prefix
const isLoading = true
const hasAccess = false
const shouldRefetch = true
const canEdit = user_id === post.author_id

// Arrays: plural nouns
const posts = []
const organizationMembers = []

// Objects: singular nouns
const user = { id: '1', name: 'John' }
```

### Functions

```typescript
// Event handlers: "handle" prefix, wrapped in useCallback
const handleSubmit = useCallback(() => {}, [])
const handleUserClick = useCallback((userId: string) => {}, [])

// Utilities: verb + noun
const formatDate = (date: Date) => { ... }
const validateEmail = (email: string) => { ... }
```

### GraphQL Exports

```typescript
// UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
export const GET_USER_BY_ID = `query ...`
export const CREATE_POST = `mutation ...`
export const MESSAGES_SUBSCRIPTION = `subscription ...`
```

