## Logging

```typescript
// utils/logger/logger.ts
type LogSource = 'GRAPHQL' | 'AUTH' | 'NAVIGATION' | 'APP'

class Logger {
  info(source: LogSource, message: string, data?: any) { ... }
  error(source: LogSource, message: string, error?: any) { ... }
  warn(source: LogSource, message: string, data?: any) { ... }
}

export const logger = new Logger()
```

### Rules

- Use `logger` instead of raw `console.log` for anything important
- Always include a source tag
- Errors automatically forwarded to Sentry
- Remove debug logs before committing

